    "result_text": "Done. The full build is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\nI made a minimal, low-impact change so every owner response carries `selfLink`:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `selfLink` string property to the `Owner` schema, which regenerates `OwnerDto` with `getSelfLink`/`setSelfLink`.\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` line deriving `selfLink` as `\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId()`.\n\nDeriving it in the shared mapper means the field is populated consistently for the create (POST), read (GET) and update (PUT) responders without touching any of the responder functions \u2014 two files touched, one changed mapper method with a single added line. The acceptance test (`createOwnerOk` \u2192 `GET /api/owners/{id}` expecting `$.selfLink == \"/api/owners/\" + id`) passes.",
